# CODEOWNERS - QTR Pairing Process
#
# When branch protection requires code-owner review, every pull request requests a
# review from the owner(s) matched by the MOST SPECIFIC rule below. Docs:
# https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repos-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# IMPORTANT - why this rule is deliberately narrow:
#
# A global rule listing several collaborators (`* @a @b @c`) does not merely
# document ownership. GitHub auto-requests a review from every matched owner on
# EVERY pull request, and each request notifies that person. On a small team where
# most pull requests come from one author, that is pure notification noise: owners
# do not opt in per-PR, and it cannot be suppressed from the PR side.
#
# Listing only the repo owner keeps this file useful for future branch protection
# while auto-requesting nobody, because GitHub never requests a review from the
# pull request's own author.
#
# If enforced team review is wanted later, prefer NARROW PATH RULES over a global
# rule, so reviewers are only pulled in on the areas they actually own. Example:
#
#   /.github/                             @dravenVTX
#   /qtr_pairing_process/db_management/   @dravenVTX
#   /setup.py                             @dravenVTX
#
# Any account listed here must have write access to the repo.

* @dravenVTX
